      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "'To create this delectable dish, start by thoroughly preparing the chicken breast, which will serve as the centerpiece. Carefully cut the chicken into uniform bite-sized pieces, ensuring each piece is evenly sized for consistent cooking. Season these pieces generously with a blend of salt, pepper, and finely minced garlic, allowing the flavors to penetrate the meat. Heat a large skillet over medium-high heat and add a generous amount of olive oil, ensuring the oil is evenly distributed across the pan's surface. Once the oil is hot, add the seasoned chicken pieces, spreading them out to ensure even cooking. Cook the chicken until it achieves a golden brown color on all sides, which should take approximately 5-7 minutes. During this time, in a separate bowl, combine heavy cream and freshly grated parmesan cheese, whisking them together to create a smooth and creamy sauce. Once the chicken is fully cooked, carefully pour the creamy sauce over the chicken pieces, stirring gently to ensure each piece is thoroughly coated. Allow the chicken to simmer in the sauce for an additional 3-4 minutes, letting the flavors meld together beautifully. To complete this dish, serve the chicken over a generous portion of pasta, ensuring that each bite is filled with the rich, savory flavors of the",
